  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening of the National Response to HIV/AIDS in Mali - Mali (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mali, HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Mali)This program has the following goals: Halve mortality in adults living with HIV by 2018 (from 13.52 deaths related to HIV / AIDS per 100 000 population in 2014 to 8.74 in 2017).  Halve new infections in adults and children exposed to HIV by 2017. The objectives of this program are: By 2017, 65% reduction of the rate of mother to child transmission among children born to HIV-infected pregnant women is expected.  By 2017, at least 90% of adults and children with HIV survive after 12 months on antiretroviral treatment.  By 2017, screen for HIV and treat with antiretroviral at least 90% of patients coinfected with TB/HIV</narrative>
  </description>
